Common Installation Mistakes to Avoid
Selecting Budget Films: Choosing low-cost, unbranded products without checking material composition.
Bypassing Paint Correction: Applying film over existing scratches or oxidation locks in paint defects.
Washing Too Soon: Cleaning the car within 7 days of installation disrupts the adhesive cure process.
Using Aggressive Cleaners: Washing film with harsh acids, solvent-heavy chemicals, or abrasive pads.
Neglecting Warranty Details: Failing to review coverage conditions, maintenance rules, or lifespan limits.
Pro Tip: Ask your detailer how they handle panel edges. Fully wrapped edges prevent visible seams and deliver a far cleaner look.

